{"word": "oversee", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "C1", "definition_en": "To watch over work and be responsible for how it is done.", "example": "A single editor oversees the whole series, which keeps the tone consistent.", "translation_he": "לפקח, לנהל"}
{"word": "perpetuate", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "C1", "definition_en": "To cause something, usually undesirable, to continue indefinitely.", "example": "Repeating the claim in textbooks perpetuates an error made in 1911.", "translation_he": "להנציח, להמשיך לקיים"}
{"word": "persecute", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "C1", "definition_en": "To treat a person or group cruelly because of their beliefs or origin.", "example": "Scholars who questioned the doctrine were persecuted for a century.", "translation_he": "לרדוף, להתנכל"}
{"word": "pioneer", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "C1", "definition_en": "To be the first to develop a method or explore an area.", "example": "Her laboratory pioneered a technique that is now standard everywhere.", "translation_he": "לחלוץ, להיות ראשון"}
{"word": "plummet", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "C1", "definition_en": "To fall very quickly and by a large amount.", "example": "Enrolment plummeted in the year the fees were introduced.", "translation_he": "לצנוח, לצלול"}
{"word": "proliferate", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "C1", "definition_en": "To increase rapidly in number and spread widely.", "example": "Unverified copies of the list proliferated faster than corrections could follow.", "translation_he": "להתרבות, להתפשט"}
