{"word": "inherit", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "To receive something from someone who came before.", "example": "Each new committee inherits the unfinished business of the last.", "translation_he": "לרשת"}
{"word": "inspect", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "To look at something closely in order to judge its condition.", "example": "Every batch is inspected by hand before it reaches the bank.", "translation_he": "לבדוק, לפקח"}
{"word": "instruct", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "To teach someone, or to tell them formally what to do.", "example": "Candidates are instructed not to return to a completed section.", "translation_he": "להורות, ללמד"}
{"word": "intrude", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "To enter or interrupt where one is not wanted.", "example": "The author's opinions intrude on what is meant to be a neutral summary.", "translation_he": "לחדור, להתפרץ"}
{"word": "linger", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "To stay longer than expected, or to be slow to disappear.", "example": "Do not linger on one question when the section is timed as a whole.", "translation_he": "להתמהמה, להישאר"}
{"word": "magnify", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "To make something appear larger, or to exaggerate its importance.", "example": "Small errors are magnified when the sample is this narrow.", "translation_he": "להגדיל, להעצים"}
{"word": "manipulate", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "To handle something skilfully, or to influence people unfairly.", "example": "The figures were manipulated to produce the expected trend.", "translation_he": "לתמרן, לתפעל"}
{"word": "merge", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "To combine two things into one.", "example": "The two archives were merged and half the duplicates disappeared.", "translation_he": "למזג, להתמזג"}
{"word": "multiply", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "To increase greatly in number.", "example": "Errors multiply once a bad assumption is built into the method.", "translation_he": "להתרבות, להכפיל"}
{"word": "navigate", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "To find a way through a place or a complicated situation.", "example": "Learning to navigate the timing is half of preparing for the exam.", "translation_he": "לנווט, למצוא דרך"}
{"word": "nourish", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "To provide what is needed to grow and stay healthy.", "example": "A good supervisor nourishes curiosity instead of correcting it away.", "translation_he": "להזין, לטפח"}
{"word": "obey", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "To do what a rule or person requires.", "example": "The system obeys the same law at every scale tested so far.", "translation_he": "לציית"}
{"word": "offend", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "To upset someone by being rude or insensitive.", "example": "The phrasing offended readers the author had not considered.", "translation_he": "לפגוע, להעליב"}
{"word": "originate", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "To begin in a particular place or from a particular source.", "example": "The convention originated in a printing limitation nobody remembers.", "translation_he": "להתחיל ב-, לנבוע מ-"}
{"word": "overlook", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "To fail to notice something, or to decide to ignore it.", "example": "Reviewers overlooked an error that a single reader later found.", "translation_he": "לפספס, להתעלם מ-"}
{"word": "overshadow", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "To make something else seem less important by comparison.", "example": "One famous result overshadowed a decade of steadier work.", "translation_he": "להאפיל על"}
{"word": "overturn", "pos": "verb", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "To reverse a decision, or to turn something upside down.", "example": "The finding overturned an assumption held since the 1950s.", "translation_he": "להפוך, לבטל החלטה"}
{"word": "achievable", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Possible to bring about with the resources available.", "example": "Three hundred validated questions by October is achievable; a thousand is not.", "translation_he": "בר-השגה"}
{"word": "adaptable", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Able to change in order to suit new conditions.", "example": "An adaptable method survives the arrival of better data.", "translation_he": "מסתגל, גמיש"}
{"word": "admirable", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Deserving respect and approval.", "example": "The restraint of the conclusion is admirable given the pressure to overclaim.", "translation_he": "ראוי להערכה"}
{"word": "anonymous", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "With a name that is not known or not revealed.", "example": "Responses are anonymous, which is why people answer honestly.", "translation_he": "אנונימי"}
{"word": "atypical", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Not conforming to the usual pattern.", "example": "The case is atypical and should not drive the general rule.", "translation_he": "חריג, לא טיפוסי"}
{"word": "bizarre", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Very strange in a way that is hard to explain.", "example": "The result was bizarre enough that the team repeated it three times.", "translation_he": "מוזר, ביזארי"}
{"word": "catastrophic", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Causing sudden and very great damage.", "example": "A catastrophic loss of records set the field back a generation.", "translation_he": "הרסני, קטסטרופלי"}
{"word": "chaotic", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Completely disordered and unpredictable.", "example": "The first week was chaotic, and nothing recorded then was usable.", "translation_he": "כאוטי, מבולגן"}
{"word": "compassionate", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Showing sympathy and a wish to help those who suffer.", "example": "A compassionate reading of the case would weigh the circumstances.", "translation_he": "רחום, אמפתי"}
{"word": "conceivable", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Possible to imagine or believe.", "example": "It is conceivable that both explanations are partly right.", "translation_he": "מתקבל על הדעת"}
{"word": "concrete", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Specific and definite rather than general or abstract.", "example": "The proposal needs concrete figures, not a statement of intent.", "translation_he": "מוחשי, קונקרטי"}
{"word": "corrupt", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Willing to act dishonestly for personal gain.", "example": "The system was not corrupt so much as badly designed.", "translation_he": "מושחת"}
{"word": "costly", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Expensive, or causing serious loss.", "example": "The delay proved costly in ways nobody had priced.", "translation_he": "יקר, כרוך בהפסד"}
{"word": "dependable", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Able to be trusted to behave as expected.", "example": "A dependable estimate matters more than a precise one here.", "translation_he": "אמין, בר-סמכא"}
{"word": "descriptive", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Giving an account of what something is like, without judging it.", "example": "The feedback is descriptive, not a grade.", "translation_he": "תיאורי"}
{"word": "dynamic", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Characterised by constant change or energetic activity.", "example": "The field is dynamic enough that a five-year-old textbook misleads.", "translation_he": "דינמי"}
{"word": "elegant", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Pleasingly graceful, or neatly simple in solving a problem.", "example": "An elegant proof replaced forty pages with half of one.", "translation_he": "אלגנטי, מעודן"}
{"word": "everlasting", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Continuing forever.", "example": "No method enjoys everlasting authority in a living discipline.", "translation_he": "נצחי"}
{"word": "expressive", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Effectively conveying thought or feeling.", "example": "A more expressive translation would keep the rhythm of the original.", "translation_he": "אקספרסיבי, מביע"}
{"word": "exquisite", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Extremely beautiful or finely made.", "example": "The exquisite detail of the binding survived four centuries.", "translation_he": "משובח, עדין ומעולה"}
{"word": "external", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Coming from or relating to the outside.", "example": "An external reviewer caught what the internal panel had missed.", "translation_he": "חיצוני"}
{"word": "fatal", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Causing death, or leading to certain failure.", "example": "The flaw was fatal to the argument, though not obvious at first.", "translation_he": "קטלני, הרה אסון"}
{"word": "faulty", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Not working correctly, or based on an error.", "example": "The conclusion rests on faulty reasoning rather than faulty data.", "translation_he": "פגום, שגוי"}
{"word": "fictional", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Invented rather than real.", "example": "The passage describes a fictional city built from three real ones.", "translation_he": "בדיוני"}
{"word": "fiscal", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Relating to public money and taxation.", "example": "The change was driven by fiscal pressure, not by evidence.", "translation_he": "פיסקלי, תקציבי"}
{"word": "flawless", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Without any fault or imperfection.", "example": "A flawless performance on the first section means little if the pacing collapses.", "translation_he": "מושלם, ללא פגם"}
{"word": "flexible", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Able to bend, or willing to change to suit circumstances.", "example": "The schedule is flexible everywhere except the examination date.", "translation_he": "גמיש"}
{"word": "constant", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Happening continuously, or staying the same over time.", "example": "The rate stayed constant across all four trials.", "translation_he": "קבוע, מתמיד"}
{"word": "determined", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Firmly resolved to do something despite difficulty.", "example": "She was determined to finish the list before the exam cycle opened.", "translation_he": "נחוש"}
{"word": "existing", "pos": "adjective", "cefr": "B2", "definition_en": "Present now, rather than planned or former.", "example": "The new rule contradicts the existing guidance in two places.", "translation_he": "קיים"}
